    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="70cefe6e-133e-509f-bc0d-114cd1e60be8" activityNameId="e578134d-f49d-5a3d-9660-1ec29e0443c1" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Inductor, ring core choke type, at plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Inductor, ring core choke type, at plant
The data represent a typical ring core choke type inductor used in the information and communication technology. Material data are taken from datasheets of producers of such inductors and from the literature. Infrastructure and production efforts are based on own assumptions. The dataset represents 1 kg of inductors with a weight of 6.0 gram/unit. No major updates were made in 2023 - according to recent product sheets from manufacturers, the composition of inductors remains similar. Production efforts dataset is update in a separate module. It is assumed that only global primary metals are used in the inventory.; UUID: 949ee0e9-1cc3-3e3b-9e81-5a933a285bb3
This dataset covers raw material input and production efforts for the production of currently used ring core choke type inductors.
Location: Data represent a global valuable composition of ring core choke type inductors.
Technology: average production comprising the following steps: core mounting; epxoy-curing; winding; welding; molding; marking; bending; testing and final control.
Time period: Unspecified
Production volume: 
Sampling: literature
Extrapolations: see Geography &amp; Technology
Uncertainty adjustments: None
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_949ee0e9-1cc3-3e3b-9e81-5a933a285bb3.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
